{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>All of them.</b> The mem is a sign [for] 'your sons.' Rabbi Moses the Kohen, of blessed memory, said that the sense of כלם is 'your sons' and 'your destroyers,' the meaning referring to the wicked, and he interpreted יצאו as a past-tense verb — but this is unnecessary:" "<b>As I live.</b> This is a decree that shall not be annulled: just as I live, so this shall come true." "<b>And you shall bind them as a bride.</b> Like a bride's ornaments on the neck."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:46.772046940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}